# Security Rules

- Treat all external input, model output, uploaded content, and third-party data as untrusted.
- Never hardcode or commit credentials, tokens, private keys, or secrets.
- Enforce authentication and authorization on the server for protected operations.
- Validate and sanitize data at trust boundaries.
- Prevent injection, unsafe redirects, insecure file handling, and accidental data exposure.
- Minimize collection, retention, and exposure of personal data.
- Do not weaken security controls to make a task pass.
- For security-sensitive changes, inspect the final diff and add targeted tests.
